#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} changed the permission overrides of the link channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} a modificat suprascrierile permisiunilor pentru canalul de tip link {channel}"

#. Activity log summary for an entry that only recorded that the permission overrides of a media channel were changed. {channel} is shown as a channel chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogForumPresentation.ts
msgid "{actor} changed the permission overrides of the media channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} a modificat suprascrierile permisiunilor canalului media {channel}"

#. Activity log summary for an older entry that only recorded that the permission overrides of a text channel were changed, without saying which. A permission override is a channel-level exception to the permissions of a role or member. It allows or denies chosen permissions in one channel or category only. Use the same word for override as the channel permissions settings, such as Add override. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts
msgid "{actor} changed the permission overrides of the text channel {channel}"
